  "question": {
    "text": "Let the digits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></math> be in A.P. Nine-digit numbers&nbsp;are to be formed using each of these three digits&nbsp;thrice such that three consecutive digits are in A.P. at least once. How many such numbers can be&nbsp;formed?"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1260",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Three numbers&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;are in A.P. ad they are used to making&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>-</mo></math>&nbsp;digit number using each digit thrice such that atleast three consecutive digits are in A.P., So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;will also be in A.P.</p><p>Now, we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;position to put&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>or</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><munder><mrow><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi></mrow><mo>&#9183;</mo></munder><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>positions</mi></mrow></munder><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math>.</p><p>Number of such numbers is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>2</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>7</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1260</mn></math></p>"
  }
